  "detail": "The factory's own review in the conflict round found this, and it is right. `runAgentGate` runs PR-controlled test code in the snapshot checkout (a standalone repository created by `exportGateSnapshot` in scratch, whose `.git` is inside the write roots), then stores the result with `putAgentGate` under the original `tree`. A test that commits in the snapshot (for example `git commit -am x` or `git reset --hard <other>` and then exit 0) leaves HEAD at a different commit, but the result is still recorded as evidence for the original tree, suppresses the round's own test run, and can satisfy verify's substitution. The gates stage already guards against exactly this (src/pipeline/engine.ts around line 1651: \"A gate may have changed HEAD itself; those results cannot attest to the checked commit\"; evidence is recorded only when `headSha(cwd) === checkedSha`). Apply the same rule here: after the execution and any retries, re-read the snapshot checkout's HEAD and HEAD's tree, and call `putAgentGate` only if HEAD still equals `head` (captured before the run) and its tree equals `tree`. Otherwise record nothing, still return the result to the session, and add a line to its output saying the result is not reusable because the snapshot changed during the gate. For the LAN executor, check the same thing on what the worker reports for the executed commit, if it reports one; if the provenance can't be confirmed, don't record (fail closed). Tests (each must fail without the fix): (a) a test command that commits in the snapshot and exits 0 \u2192 no record, the gates stage runs the test check, and verify does not substitute it; (b) a test command that resets HEAD to another commit \u2192 no record; (c) the unchanged-HEAD case still records and reuses. Run only test/agent-full-suite-gate.test.ts test/agent-test.test.ts test/gate-evidence.test.ts test/git-integrity.test.ts test/lan-agent.test.ts test/pipeline-slotted.test.ts test/gate-docs-only.test.ts, `bunx biome check` on the changed files and `bunx tsc --noEmit`. Never run the full suite in a factory run (AGENTS.md)."
